{"node_id": "LVMC_11_38_030", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-38-030"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle", "ru.moped", "ru.electric_scooter"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "No motorcycle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "or motor scooter", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall be ridden upon any sidewalk", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "of the City", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definitions table admits 'motorcycle' as the aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground, excluding an electric bicycle, a tractor or a moped'). ru.aggregate is 'membership of a legal aggregate' and is claimed whole, never expanded into ru.motorcycle. Its 'not a stand-in for' clauses do not apply: the words name a class, not a role described by conduct or a relational role. The word 'No' negates the duty the obligation span s3 states."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.moped", "ru.electric_scooter"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Motor scooter' has no applicable definition, so its words are mapped by contract. A scooter driven by a motor is, in the taxonomy the corpus posts, either a moped (DEF-NRS-484A-125: 'a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle' with a small engine; ru.moped: 'a low-power two- or three-wheeler with a small engine or motor, as a jurisdiction classes it') or an electric scooter (DEF-NRS-484A-082: 'a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'; ru.electric_scooter: 'a standing or seated electric scooter with handlebars'). A motor scooter above the moped's power is a motorcycle under DEF-NRS-484A-135 and is carried by s1. The ontology carries no body-style attribute, so a moped of cycle body is read with the scooters the moped definition groups it with. Neither class atom carries a 'not a stand-in for' clause."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.sidewalk", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving"], "justification": "'Sidewalk' (DEF-NRS-484A-240: 'that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians') is st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line'; its exclusion (not a crosswalk) applies as the definition does: a crosswalk lies across the roadway and is not that portion. 'upon any sidewalk' places the subject on the feature, anchored by rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... sidewalk ...)', for every sidewalk region of the scene. 'ridden' is read through the machine's controlled motion: drv.motion.moving (the road user in motion beyond the speed resolution); a machine standing on the sidewalk is not being ridden."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [{"span": "s4", "id": "asm.within_city_limits", "meaning": "The place of the observation lies within the territorial limits of an incorporated city."}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle", "ru.moped", "ru.electric_scooter"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the motorcycle aggregate (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle) or carries ru.moped or ru.electric_scooter, and asm.within_city_limits holds.", "obligation": "Not (drv.motion.moving(x; p.motion_speed_tolerance) and existsRegion st.sidewalk s: rel.occupies(x, s)): at the observation x is not in motion while its footprint overlaps any sidewalk region.", "params": ["p.motion_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s3", "why": "'ridden' (who or what rides the machine is not observable) is read through the machine's controlled motion: the machine in motion with its footprint on a sidewalk is ridden there; a machine pushed along the sidewalk is read the same way.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A motorcycle (ru.motorcycle, an included class of the aggregate) moves along a sidewalk: its footprint overlaps a st.sidewalk region and kin.speed is above the tolerance; asm.within_city_limits is declared true."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same motorcycle moves along the roadway beside the sidewalk; rel.occupies holds for the st.roadway and for no st.sidewalk region; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A bicycle (ru.bicycle: neither in the motorcycle aggregate nor a moped or electric scooter) is ridden along the sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A motorcycle moves beside a sidewalk; the source declares rel.occupies absent, so whether its footprint overlaps the sidewalk is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A motorcycle stands parked on the sidewalk: kin.speed is zero at every observation; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A moped (ru.moped) moves along the sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A motorcycle moves along a sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits is declared false."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_A", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-A"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to the", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "operation of vehicles", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "within a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "All vehicular travel", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "shall be in a counterclockwise direction", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definitions table admits 'vehicle' as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', with its exceptions); ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate', claimed whole. It is not a relational role: 'operation' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.roundabout", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Roundabout' (DEF-LVMC-11-02-130: 'an intersection characterized by a circulatory roadway, channelized approaches and yield control of entering traffic', encompassing 'the area bounded by the outermost curb line') is st.roundabout: 'a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches'; the atom has no 'not a stand-in for' clause, and the defined word keeps its whole extent, approaches and crosswalks included. 'within' places the subject in the feature: rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving"], "justification": "'vehicular' is the admitted vehicle aggregate (claimed whole); 'travel' is the vehicle's motion, drv.motion.moving: in motion beyond the speed resolution. A vehicle standing in the roundabout is not travelling."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.clockwise_about_region"], "justification": "Counterclockwise travel within a roundabout is travel around its central island (DEF-LVMC-11-02-040: the circulatory roadway is 'used by vehicles to travel counterclockwise around a central island'). drv.motion.clockwise_about_region, called on the roundabout region x occupies, denotes motion clockwise about the region's reference point; the duty is that it does not hold. The concept reads velocity, not heading, so a vehicle backing clockwise around the island is caught, and radial travel on an approach (entering, leaving) has no clockwise component."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate, drv.motion.moving(x; p.motion_speed_tolerance) holds, and existsRegion st.roundabout r: rel.occupies(x, r).", "obligation": "forallRegion st.roundabout r: rel.occupies(x, r) implies not drv.motion.clockwise_about_region(x, r; p.motion_speed_tolerance). The roundabout is re-bound in the obligation with the same selection (a roundabout region x's footprint overlaps), so each roundabout x is within is the one judged.", "params": ["p.motion_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'operation of vehicles' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion; who or what controls it is not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'in a counterclockwise direction' is read as: no motion clockwise about the roundabout's reference point beyond the speed resolution. Radial motion (entering or leaving along an approach) is not clockwise and complies. The roundabout region's reference point (st.region_geometry) is read as the centre the circulatory roadway runs around.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car (an included class of the vehicle aggregate) occupies a st.roundabout region and moves around the central island clockwise: the cross product of its offset from the region's reference point and its kin.velocity is negative with a tangential speed above the tolerance."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car moves around the island counterclockwise within the roundabout region."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car moves along a straight roadway; no st.roundabout region is in the scene."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A car occupies a roundabout region and moves clockwise around the island; the source maps the region without its outline and reference point (st.region_geometry absent), so the sense of rotation is unknown.", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car on the right-hand entry approach inside the roundabout region moves straight toward the island; its tangential component about the reference point is counterclockwise or below the tolerance."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car stands still inside the roundabout region, yielding: kin.speed is zero."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_113_2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-113-2"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "Shall not back", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "into an intersection", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "on or over a crosswalk", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "or around a", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "street", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "corner", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'). 'The driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080: 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle') is a relational role, which ru.aggregate is 'not a stand-in for'; it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, so the duty binds the vehicle's conduct (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.backing"], "justification": "'back' is the vehicle moving backwards: drv.motion.backing, its velocity along the direction it points below minus the speed resolution. The concept reads kinematics, not kin.gear, whose contract is 'not a stand-in for: the direction of motion ... backing is read from kinematics'. The places the words name (s3 to s7) are read as conditions of the same observation, so the forbidden act is backing at one of them."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.intersection", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Intersection' (DEF-NRS-484A-105: 'the area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines ... of the roadways of two highways'; the junction of an alley is none) is st.intersection: 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges; a junction where an alley meets another way ... is no intersection'. Its exclusions (not a crosswalk or a stop line) hold: the words name the junction itself. 'into' is the entry: the observation at which rel.occupies(x, i) ('a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') becomes true (rises)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Crosswalk' (DEF-NRS-484A-065: the unmarked part at an intersection within the prolonged sidewalk lines, or 'any portion of a highway ... distinctly indicated for pedestrian crossing by lines or other markings') is st.crosswalk: 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection', both senses. 'on or over' is the footprint overlapping it at the observation: rel.occupies."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.turning"], "justification": "'around' a corner is a path that bends: the vehicle's heading is changing at the observation, drv.motion.turning (yaw-rate magnitude above its resolution). kin.yaw_rate is 'not a stand-in for road curvature'; the concept reads the vehicle's own yaw, not the road."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.intersection", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "A street corner is the corner where two streets meet, which lies at the boundary of the intersection region (st.intersection: 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges'); a vehicle rounding it overlaps that region (rel.occupies)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [{"span": "s6", "id": "asm.within_city_limits", "meaning": "The place of the observation lies within the territorial limits of an incorporated city."}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate and at least one of: (a) existsRegion st.intersection i: rises(rel.occupies(x, i)) - x enters an intersection at this observation; (b) existsRegion st.crosswalk c: rel.occupies(x, c); (c) asm.within_city_limits and drv.motion.turning(x; p.yaw_rate_tolerance) and existsRegion st.intersection j: rel.occupies(x, j) - x rounds a street corner.", "obligation": "not drv.motion.backing(x; p.motion_speed_tolerance) at the observation.", "params": ["p.motion_speed_tolerance", "p.yaw_rate_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion; who or what controls the vehicle is not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "Each place is read at the observation: 'into an intersection' as backing at the observation at which the footprint begins to overlap the intersection (backing further within an intersection already entered is not 'into'); 'on or over a crosswalk' as backing while the footprint overlaps a crosswalk; 'around a street corner' as backing while yawing with the footprint on an intersection inside a city (street: DEF-NRS-484A-265 'every highway inside the territorial limits of a city'). A corner rounded without the footprint touching the intersection region is not read.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car moves backwards (kin.velocity opposite kin.heading) and at this observation its footprint begins to overlap a st.intersection region."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car drives forwards into the intersection."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car backs straight along a roadway mid-block; no intersection or crosswalk is overlapped and it is not yawing."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A car enters an intersection; the source declares kin.velocity absent, so whether it is backing is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.velocity"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car backs over a marked mid-block st.crosswalk (no intersection)."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Having entered an intersection forwards, a car backs while yawing round its corner, its footprint on the intersection and on no crosswalk; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As branch_2, with asm.within_city_limits false: the corner is no street corner, the car entered forwards and overlaps no crosswalk."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}, {"name": "p.yaw_rate_tolerance", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Yaw-rate resolution: the noise floor of a source's yaw-rate estimate, below which a heading is read as not changing.", "source": "Vehicle IMU and tracker yaw-rate noise figures."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_127_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-127-3"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Motor vehicles", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "being driven", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "upon any highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "outside of a business district", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "in a caravan or motorcade", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "whether or not towing other vehicles", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "shall be operated to allow", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "sufficient space between each such vehicle or combination of vehicles so as to enable any other vehicle or combination of vehicles to enter and occupy such space without danger", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definitions table admits 'motor vehicle' as DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle ('every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails'); ru.aggregate is claimed whole, never replaced by ru.motor_vehicle, whose own contract says it is 'not a stand-in for: \"vehicle\" as a legal aggregate'."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving"], "justification": "'being driven' is the vehicle in controlled motion (agency reading): drv.motion.moving, in motion beyond the speed resolution; the progressive form places the caravan in motion."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.highway", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Highway' (DEF-NRS-484A-095: 'the entire width between the boundary lines of every way dedicated to a public authority') is st.highway: 'the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders'; its exclusion ('not a stand-in for the roadway') holds, as the words name the whole way. 'upon' anchors the subject: rel.occupies."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap"], "derived": [], "justification": "'operated to allow ... space between each such vehicle' is the space the subject keeps to the vehicle ahead of it in the line: rel.ahead_behind_in_lane ('a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction') selects that vehicle and rel.surface_gap ('distance between the nearest points of two bodies') measures the space, rather than rel.centre_distance, which is 'not a stand-in for a clearance between bodies'. 'operated' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency)."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "sufficient space ... so as to enable any other vehicle or combination of vehicles to enter and occupy such space without danger", "concepts": ["rel.surface_gap", "rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "kin.speed", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles"], "params": ["p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length", "p.caravan_entry_time_headway"], "convention": "Gap-acceptance convention for a merging vehicle: the space must hold the entering design vehicle (the longest combination of vehicles, so that 'any other vehicle or combination' fits) plus an accepted time headway ahead of it and another behind it at the caravan's speed. The bound is p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length plus p.caravan_entry_time_headway times x's kin.speed, the headway term counted once for the gap ahead of the entering vehicle and once for the gap behind it; the bound grows with the speed, so the degree of the speed factor is read. 'each such vehicle or combination of vehicles' is the road user ahead in the lane, a member of the vehicle aggregate or of the combination-of-vehicles aggregate.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [{"span": "s4", "id": "asm.outside_business_district", "meaning": "The stretch of highway at the observation lies outside every territory classed as a business district."}, {"span": "s5", "id": "asm.caravan_or_motorcade", "meaning": "The motor vehicles of the trace that travel one behind another in the same lane travel together as an organised caravan or motorcade."}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s6", "why": "The words extend the duty to vehicles towing others and to those not towing alike: whether a caravan vehicle tows adds no condition, and a towed unit ahead is already a member of the vehicle or combination-of-vehicles aggregate the obligation reads.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the motor-vehicle aggregate, drv.motion.moving(x; p.motion_speed_tolerance) holds, existsRegion st.highway h: rel.occupies(x, h), and asm.outside_business_district and asm.caravan_or_motorcade hold.", "obligation": "forallUser y: (not same(x, y) and (ru.aggregate(y, DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) or ru.aggregate(y, DEF-NRS-484A-050::combination_of_vehicles)) and rel.ahead_behind_in_lane(y, x)) implies rel.surface_gap(x, y) >= p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length + p.caravan_entry_time_headway * kin.speed(x) + p.caravan_entry_time_headway * kin.speed(x). With no road user ahead in the lane the duty is met.", "params": ["p.motion_speed_tolerance", "p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length", "p.caravan_entry_time_headway"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s7", "why": "'operated' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the space it keeps to the vehicle ahead in its lane.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "'without danger' is read only through the time headway the entering vehicle keeps ahead of and behind it at the subject's speed; the closing speed of the vehicle ahead, the road surface and the sight distance are not read. 'any other vehicle or combination of vehicles' is read through the length of the design combination, the longest an entrant may be.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Two cars travel one behind the other in the same lane of a highway at cruising speed; asm.caravan_or_motorcade and asm.outside_business_district are true; the follower's rel.surface_gap to the leader is about one car length, below the bound."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, with the follower's surface gap well above the design length plus both headways at its speed."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, with asm.outside_business_district false (the stretch is in a business district)."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, with rel.surface_gap declared absent by the source.", "masked": ["rel.surface_gap"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A single car moves on the highway with both assumptions true and no road user ahead of it in its lane: the duty binds it and is met."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, with asm.caravan_or_motorcade false."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}, {"name": "p.caravan_entry_vehicle_length", "unit": "m", "value": 22.4, "convention": "Overall length of the longest design combination a highway is designed for (an interstate semitrailer combination), so that any vehicle or combination can occupy the space.", "source": "AASHTO A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets, WB-67 design vehicle overall length."}, {"name": "p.caravan_entry_time_headway", "unit": "s", "value": 1.0, "convention": "Minimum accepted lead and lag time gap of a merging or lane-changing vehicle, applied once ahead of and once behind the entering vehicle.", "source": "Lane-change gap-acceptance studies (critical lead and lag gaps of about one second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_210_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-210-3"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "when such movement requires driving off the paved portion of the highway", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'). 'The driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080) is a relational role, which ru.aggregate is 'not a stand-in for'; it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.passing_on_right"], "justification": "'overtake and pass ... upon the right' is drv.interaction.passing_on_right(x, y): the two heading the same way, side by side, y on x's left, x gaining on y. 'another vehicle' is the admitted vehicle aggregate, claimed whole, for the road user y passed, quantified inside the obligation (a party present only when one is there)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.shoulder", "st.road_edge", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'driving off the paved portion of the highway' is the vehicle's footprint on an unpaved surface of the way: st.shoulder ('the part of the highway beside the roadway not intended for vehicular traffic; paved attribute') with paved false, or st.road_edge ('curb or edge of the roadway; paved attribute for the surface beyond it') whose surface beyond is unpaved and which the footprint straddles; rel.occupies anchors the subject on that feature. Neither atom carries a 'not a stand-in for' clause. 'requires' is read through the conduct: the movement made while off the pavement."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate and is off the paved portion: (existsRegion st.shoulder s: rel.occupies(x, s) and the paved attribute of s is false) or (existsRegion st.road_edge e: rel.occupies(x, e) and the paved attribute of e, for the surface beyond it, is false).", "obligation": "forallUser y: (not same(x, y) and ru.aggregate(y, DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle)) implies not drv.interaction.passing_on_right(x, y; p.same_direction_cos_tolerance, p.motion_speed_tolerance). With no other vehicle beside x the duty is met.", "params": ["p.same_direction_cos_tolerance", "p.motion_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion; who or what controls the vehicle is not observable.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "The pass is judged at each observation of its side-by-side phase in which x, gaining on a vehicle on its left, is off the pavement; 'requires driving off the paved portion' is read through that conduct, so a pass that would have required leaving the pavement but was not made is not read, and an off-pavement position that is neither an unpaved shoulder nor a straddled unpaved edge is not read.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car's footprint overlaps an unpaved st.shoulder; a slower car travels the same way in the adjacent lane on its left; their footprints overlap along the subject's heading and the subject is gaining."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car on the unpaved shoulder moves slower than the car beside it on its left: it is being passed, not passing."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car passes a slower car on its right within the paved roadway; no unpaved shoulder or edge is overlapped."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, with rel.longitudinal_overlap declared absent, so whether the two are side by side is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car moves alone along the unpaved shoulder; no other road user is in the scene."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.same_direction_cos_tolerance", "unit": "1", "value": 0.9, "convention": "Heading alignment: cosine of the largest angle between two headings still read as the same way of travel (about a quarter of a right angle), covering lane changes and road bends.", "source": "Lane-change trajectory geometry in naturalistic driving data."}, {"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_223_4a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-223-4a"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "If a highway has been designed to provide a single right lane to be used only for turning", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "must: Be driven in the right turn lane only", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "for the purpose of making a right turn", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["st.turn_lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a right lane to be used only for turning' is st.turn_lane: 'a lane designated only for turning; side ∈ {left, right}', side right. 'single right lane' is the rightmost lane of its direction (st.lane_adjacency: 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane', so ordinal equals count) whose left neighbour of the same direction is not itself a right turn lane; st.lane_adjacency is 'not a stand-in for the marking between two lanes', which is not read. 'a highway' (DEF-NRS-484A-095) is st.highway, the way x is on (rel.occupies anchors it), and st.on_way ('the public way ... a structure region lies on') ties the lane to that highway. 'has been designed to provide' is read through the lane's presence (status reading)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'); it names a class, not a role."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.turn_lane", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Be driven in the right turn lane' is the vehicle's footprint on the lane s1 selects, re-bound with that whole selection: rel.occupies ('a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') on st.turn_lane side right. The turn the lane serves is made at the intersection the lane runs into: st.lane_enters ('the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end'), whose st.intersection region is the target of the declared purpose; st.lane_enters is 'not a stand-in for the lane a lane leads into', which is not read. 'driven' is read through the vehicle's controlled presence on the road (agency). 'must ... only' makes the purpose (s4) the only case in which the presence is allowed."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s4", "id": "int.turn_right", "meaning": "The road user's current plan includes a right turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate and existsRegion st.highway h: rel.occupies(x, h) and existsRegion st.turn_lane L: L's side is right, st.on_way(L, h), L is the rightmost lane of its direction (st.lane_adjacency ordinal equals count) and its left neighbour of the same direction is not a right turn lane.", "obligation": "For every lane L re-bound with the whole selection of the applicability (a right turn lane, single and rightmost, on a highway h x occupies) with rel.occupies(x, L): existsRegion st.intersection i: st.lane_enters(L, i) and intent(int.turn_right, x, i) at the judged observation. Where the source records no intersection L enters, the target is not observed and the verdict is unknown (definedWhen on the existence of the entrance), never violated for want of a record.", "params": [], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'has been designed to provide' (the lane's legal designation) is read through the marked turn lane's presence on the highway.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'driven' is read through the vehicle's presence in the lane: a vehicle on the road is taken to be driven, standing in a queue included.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car's footprint overlaps the single right turn lane of a highway; the source declares int.turn_right false for it at the intersection the lane enters (its plan goes straight on)."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, with int.turn_right declared true at that intersection."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car drives on a highway with no turn lane on it."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A car drives beside and possibly within the right turn lane; rel.occupies is declared absent.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car drives in the through lane beside the single right turn lane; no intention is declared for it."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The highway has two adjacent right turn lanes (no single right turn lane); a car in the rightmost one has int.turn_right declared false."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_223_4b", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-223-4b"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "If a highway has been designed to provide a single right lane to be used only for turning", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "must: While being driven in the right turn lane, not travel through an intersection", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["st.turn_lane", "st.lane_adjacency", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a right lane to be used only for turning' is st.turn_lane: 'a lane designated only for turning; side ∈ {left, right}', side right. 'single right lane' is the rightmost lane of its direction (st.lane_adjacency: 'lane ordinal within the carriageway and the count of lanes in that direction; ordinal 1 is the leftmost lane', so ordinal equals count) whose left neighbour of the same direction is not itself a right turn lane; st.lane_adjacency is 'not a stand-in for the marking between two lanes', which is not read. 'a highway' (DEF-NRS-484A-095) is st.highway, the way x is on (rel.occupies anchors it), and st.on_way ('the public way ... a structure region lies on') ties the lane to that highway. 'has been designed to provide' is read through the lane's presence (status reading)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'); it names a class, not a role."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.turn_lane", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.straight_through_region"], "justification": "'travel through an intersection' is drv.motion.straight_through_region(x, i): x leaves the intersection region with a heading change since its entry below the turn bound, called on the intersection i the right turn lane runs into (st.lane_enters: 'the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end'; st.intersection: 'the region where two roadways meet'). 'While being driven in the right turn lane' ties the crossing to the lane: x's footprint overlapped that lane (rel.occupies on the st.turn_lane s1 selects, re-bound) at some observation since its entry into i, that is, it entered i out of the lane. st.lane_enters is 'not a stand-in for the lane a lane leads into' or for x's presence in the intersection, which rel.occupies reads."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate and existsRegion st.highway h: rel.occupies(x, h) and existsRegion st.turn_lane L: L's side is right, st.on_way(L, h), L is the rightmost lane of its direction (st.lane_adjacency ordinal equals count) and its left neighbour of the same direction is not a right turn lane.", "obligation": "Not (existsRegion st.turn_lane L, re-bound with the whole selection of s1 (side right, on a highway, single and rightmost), and existsRegion st.intersection i: st.lane_enters(L, i) and drv.motion.straight_through_region(x, i; p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, p.straight_through_max_heading_change) and rel.occupies(x, L) held at some observation since x's entry into i, the observation at which rel.occupies(x, i) last rose). The act is judged at its recognition, the observation at which x leaves i.", "params": ["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.straight_through_max_heading_change"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'has been designed to provide' (the lane's legal designation) is read through the marked turn lane's presence on the highway.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'travel through' is read as leaving the intersection the lane enters with a heading change since the entry below the turn bound (a straight crossing); 'While being driven in the right turn lane' is read as the footprint overlapping that lane at some observation of the crossing, which it does at the entry made out of the lane. A vehicle in the lane is taken to be driven (agency).", "kind": "reading"}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.motion.straight_through_region", "boundary": "event", "onset": {"words": "travel through an intersection", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "The crossing begins at the entry: the observation at which rel.occupies(x, i) last became true for the intersection i the lane enters."}, "recognition": "The observation at which x's footprint stops overlapping the intersection it entered, with its heading change since the entry below the turn bound.", "under_way": {"words": "travel through an intersection", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": [], "justification": "An observation is inside the crossing where it lies from the entry onwards and the heading change since the entry is being integrated from kin.yaw_rate; before the entry nothing is integrated, so the motion read, not the region alone, tells the inside of the act from what precedes it."}, "spans": {"s1": "at_recognition"}}, "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car in the single right turn lane enters the intersection the lane runs into and leaves it on the far side heading as it entered (heading change since entry below the bound)."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same car turns right in the intersection and leaves it heading to the right of its entry heading."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A highway without any turn lane; a car crosses an intersection straight."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "