rv.motion.u_turn"], "justification": "The 'must not' of the preceding words governs this list ('must not be driven over ... or make any ...'). 'left turn' is drv.motion.left_turn (heading change to the left over the recognition window, short of a reversal); 'U-turn' (DEF-NRS-484B-077: 'the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not') is drv.motion.u_turn; a 'semicircular turn' turns the vehicle through a half circle so that it proceeds the opposite way, a reversal of heading that drv.motion.u_turn recognizes however the turn is made."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["st.median_or_divider", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'an opening in the barrier or dividing section or space' is the st.median_or_divider region carrying its 'opening attribute where a crossover exists'; 'through' it is the footprint overlapping that opening region (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.median_or_divider", "st.intersection", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'a crossover' is the divider's opening (st.median_or_divider: 'opening attribute where a crossover exists'); 'intersection' (DEF-NRS-484A-105; on a divided highway 'every crossing of each roadway ... shall be regarded as a separate intersection') is st.intersection: 'the region where two roadways meet', 'not a stand-in for a crosswalk or a stop line', neither of which is read. 'at' is the footprint overlapping the opening or the intersection (rel.occupies). 'established by a public authority' is read through the feature's presence (status reading)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a member of the vehicle aggregate and either x occupies a divided highway at the observation (existsRegion st.highway h: rel.occupies(x, h) and existsRegion st.median_or_divider m: st.on_way(m, h)), or it did so at some observation of the window of p.turn_recognition_window behind at which drv.motion.turning(x; p.yaw_rate_tolerance) held (some moment of a turn under way).", "obligation": "At an observation at which drv.motion.left_turn(x; p.turn_recognition_window, p.left_turn_min_angle, p.reversal_min_angle) or drv.motion.u_turn(x; p.turn_recognition_window, p.reversal_min_angle, p.reversal_max_angle) rises (the act's recognition), the act is excepted only where, at some observation of the window of p.turn_recognition_window behind at which drv.motion.turning(x; p.yaw_rate_tolerance) held, x's footprint overlapped a st.median_or_divider region whose opening attribute holds or a st.intersection region; otherwise violated. At observations at which neither act rises the duty is met.", "params": ["p.turn_recognition_window", "p.left_turn_min_angle", "p.reversal_min_angle", "p.reversal_max_angle", "p.yaw_rate_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'driven' is read through the vehicle's presence on the road: a vehicle on the road is taken to be driven.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "'established by a public authority' (the legal status of the crossover or intersection) is read through the opening's or the intersection's presence on the road.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "The turns are recognized over a window of fixed length: a turn or reversal that takes longer than the window is not recognized, and the moments of the act are read as the turning observations of that window, which may include a separate turn made just before.", "kind": "reading"}], "occasion": {"act": ["drv.motion.left_turn", "drv.motion.u_turn"], "boundary": "window", "window": "p.turn_recognition_window", "under_way": {"words": "or make any left turn, semicircular turn or U-turn", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.turning"], "justification": "An observation is inside the turn where it lies in the recognition window behind the act's recognition and the vehicle's heading is changing there (drv.motion.turning, its yaw rate above the resolution); observations of the window at which it drives straight, before the turn began, are not inside it."}, "spans": {"s2": "some_moment", "s6": "some_moment", "s7": "some_moment"}}, "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a divided highway a car makes a U-turn within its right-hand roadway between intersections, nowhere near a median opening: heading reverses within the window; no intersection or opening is overlapped while it turns."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car drives straight along the right-hand roadway of the divided highway; no turn rises."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car makes a U-turn on an undivided highway; it was on no divided highway in the window."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, with kin.yaw_rate declared absent, so the heading change over the window is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}, {"name": "occasion_s2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car begins a left turn on the divided highway mid-block, crossing toward a side driveway without an opening, and completes the turn off the divided highway; it was on the divided highway at turning observations of the window."}, {"name": "occasion_s2_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A car leaves the divided highway onto an undivided road, drives straight on it, then turns left there; at no turning observation of the window was it on the divided highway."}, {"name": "occasion_s6", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car makes a U-turn through a median opening: at some turning observations its footprint overlaps the median region whose opening attribute holds."}, {"name": "occasion_s6_outside", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car drives straight past and over a median opening region, then later, mid-block, reverses its heading within the roadway; while it turns it overlaps no opening and no intersection."}, {"name": "occasion_s7", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car turns left at an intersection of the divided highway: its footprint overlaps the st.intersection region at turning observations."}, {"name": "occasion_s7_outside", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car drives straight through an intersection, then mid-block makes a U-turn within the roadway; while it turns it overlaps no intersection and no opening."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.turn_recognition_window", "unit": "s", "value": 15.0, "convention": "The time within which a turn or a reversal, a reversal made in several moves included, is completed: the window over which the heading change that recognizes it is measured.", "source": "Intersection turning times and three-point-turn durations in naturalistic driving data."}, {"name": "p.left_turn_min_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 60.0, "convention": "The heading change to the left beyond which a manoeuvre is a turn rather than a lane change or a bend's drift.", "source": "Turning-movement classification practice in trajectory studies."}, {"name": "p.reversal_min_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 150.0, "convention": "The heading change magnitude from which the heading has come round to the opposite direction (a reversal); also the upper end of a left turn's band.", "source": "U-turn classification practice in trajectory studies."}, {"name": "p.reversal_max_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 210.0, "convention": "The heading change magnitude beyond which the heading has come round past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).", "source": "U-turn classification practice in trajectory studies."}, {"name": "p.yaw_rate_tolerance", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Yaw-rate resolution: the noise floor of a source's yaw-rate estimate, below which a heading is read as not changing.", "source": "Vehicle IMU and tracker yaw-rate noise figures."}], "gaps": []}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.moving", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user is in motion at the observation: the magnitude of its velocity (kin.speed) exceeds `tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as standing still. It denotes motion in any direction, forwards or backwards, whoever or whatever controls the road user. Not denoted: the direction of motion; a halt held over a window, since the concept reads the one observation.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "The source's speed resolution: a speed at or below it counts as standing still."}], "elements": [{"span": "the magnitude of its velocity (kin.speed)", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.speed: 'magnitude of velocity', m/s; it carries no direction, which the concept does not need."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car's kin.speed is well above the tolerance."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car stands: kin.speed is zero."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The source declares kin.speed absent.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_38_030", "LVMC_11_43_010_A", "NRS_484B_127_3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.backing", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user moves backwards at the observation: the component of its velocity (kin.velocity) along the direction it points (kin.heading) is below minus `tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's speed resolution. Not denoted: the gear selected, since a vehicle in reverse gear standing still is not backing and one rolling backwards in a forward gear is; motion across the direction it points, such as a sideways slide; a road user standing still.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "The source's speed resolution: a backward component at or below it in magnitude counts as none."}], "elements": [{"span": "the component of its velocity (kin.velocity)", "atoms": ["kin.velocity"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.velocity: 'velocity vector', m/s, world frame; its dot product with the heading is the signed motion along the body's axis."}, {"span": "the direction it points (kin.heading)", "atoms": ["kin.heading"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.heading: 'direction the body points', a unit vector read normalised; a zero vector reads unknown."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car's velocity points opposite its heading with a magnitude above the tolerance."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car moves forwards: its velocity points along its heading."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The source declares kin.velocity absent.", "masked": ["kin.velocity"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_113_2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.turning", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user's heading is changing at the observation: the magnitude of its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) exceeds `tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's yaw-rate resolution, to either hand and whether the road user moves forwards or backwards. Not denoted: the curvature of the road, which the concept does not read; a completed turn or the angle turned; the hand of the turn.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "tol", "unit": "deg/s", "meaning": "The source's yaw-rate resolution: a yaw rate at or below it in magnitude counts as none."}], "elements": [{"span": "the magnitude of its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate)", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: 'rate of change of heading', deg/s, signed; its magnitude is turning to either hand. It is 'not a stand-in for road curvature': the concept reads the road user's own yaw."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car rounds a corner with a yaw rate well above the tolerance."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car drives straight: its yaw rate is zero."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The source declares kin.yaw_rate absent.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_113_2", "NRS_484B_227_1_o3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.clockwise_about_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user moves clockwise about a region's reference point at the observation: seen from above in the world frame, in the sense opposite to the one in which the ontology counts a left turn as counter-clockwise, the component of its velocity (kin.velocity) perpendicular to the line from the region's reference point (st.region_geometry) to the road user's reference point (kin.position) points clockwise about the region's reference point, and that component's magnitude exceeds `tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's speed resolution. It is computed from the cross product c of the offset of the road user's reference point from the region's reference point with the velocity (the offset's first component times the velocity's second, minus the offset's second component times the velocity's first), negative for clockwise motion: the concept holds where c is negative and c times c exceeds tol times tol times the squared length of the offset. Not denoted: the direction the road user points, since a vehicle backing clockwise moves clockwise; motion toward or away from the reference point, such as entering or leaving; whether the road user occupies the region, which the caller states; the designated direction of any carrier.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "The source's speed resolution: a tangential speed at or below it counts as no rotation."}], "elements": [{"span": "its velocity (kin.velocity)", "atoms": ["kin.velocity"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.velocity: 'velocity vector', m/s, world frame."}, {"span": "the region's reference point (st.region_geometry)", "atoms": ["st.region_geometry"], "concepts": [], "justification": "st.region_geometry: 'the reference point and the boundary polygon of a structure region in the world frame'."}, {"span": "the road user's reference point (kin.position)", "atoms": ["kin.position"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.position: 'position of the body's reference point', m, world frame."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car circles a roundabout's island clockwise at speed: the cross product is negative and its tangential speed exceeds the tolerance."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The car circles the island counterclockwise."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The region is mapped without its reference point (st.region_geometry absent).", "masked": ["st.region_geometry"]}], "used_by": ["LVMC_11_43_010_A"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.interaction.passing_on_right", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user a is passing road user b on b's right at the observation: the two head the same way (rel.same_direction with cosine tolerance `cos_tol`), their footprints overlap along a's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap not negative, so the two are side by side), b lies to a's left (the lateral component of rel.bearing from a to b is positive, left positive), and a's speed (kin.speed) exceeds b's by more than `speed_tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's speed resolution. It holds at each observation of the side-by-side phase in which a gains on b. Not denoted: the approach from behind before the footprints overlap, or the moment a draws clear ahead; a pass on b's left; b gaining on a; a lane change; where either road user is, which the caller states.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "a", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "b", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "cos_tol", "unit": "1", "meaning": "Cosine of the largest angle between the two headings still read as the same way."}, {"name": "speed_tol", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "The source's speed resolution: a speed difference at or below it counts as none."}], "elements": [{"span": "the two head the same way (rel.same_direction with cosine tolerance `cos_tol`)", "atoms": ["rel.same_direction"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.same_direction: 'headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance'."}, {"span": "their footprints overlap along a's heading (rel.longitudinal_overlap not negative", "atoms": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.longitudinal_overlap: 'the bodies overlap along the subject's heading (side by side)', negative for the gap between the projections."}, {"span": "b lies to a's left (the lateral component of rel.bearing from a to b is positive", "atoms": ["rel.bearing"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.bearing: 'direction of b from a in a's frame (for \"on the right of\" ...)'."}, {"span": "a's speed (kin.speed) exceeds b's", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.speed: 'magnitude of velocity'; with the headings aligned, the faster one gains."}], "residues": [], "literals": [{"value": "0", "unit": "m", "why": "The overlap bound: an overlap not negative is the two side by side, a geometric constant."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Car a, on the right of car b and side by side with it, both heading the same way, moves faster than b."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Car a is side by side with b on b's right but slower than b."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with rel.longitudinal_overlap declared absent.", "masked": ["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_210_3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.straight_through_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user has travelled straight through a region, such as an intersection the caller passes: at the observation it leaves the region (its footprint overlaps the region, rel.occupies, at the observation before and not at this one), and the magnitude of its heading change since its entry, the observation at which the overlap last became true, integrated from its yaw rate with sampling step bound `step`, is below `max_angle`, the heading change below which a crossing counts as straight. The act begins at the entry, the observation at which the overlap last became true. The act is recognized at the observation it leaves the region. The concept holds only at the exit observation, ending at the next observation. Conduct before the entry is not read. Not denoted: a turn, a heading change at or beyond `max_angle`; a road user still within the region; which carrier it entered from, which the caller states; a crossing whose entry the recording does not show, for which the heading change since entry is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "i", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "step", "unit": "ms", "meaning": "The sampling step bound of the heading-change integration: the largest gap between consecutive observations it integrates across."}, {"name": "max_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The heading change since entry below which a crossing counts as straight."}], "act": {"boundary": "event", "onset": "The act begins at the entry, the observation at which the overlap last became true.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation it leaves the region.", "extent": "The concept holds only at the exit observation, ending at the next observation.", "history": "Conduct before the entry is not read."}, "elements": [{"span": "its footprint overlaps the region, rel.occupies", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; its fall is the exit and its last rise the entry."}, {"span": "integrated from its yaw rate", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: 'rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left'; Term.headingSince integrates it from the entry."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car enters an intersection and leaves it on the far side heading as it entered."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car enters an intersection, turns right and leaves it."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with kin.yaw_rate declared absent.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_223_4b"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.lane.facing_against_direction", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user points against the designated direction of travel of a carrier at the observation: the cosine of the angle between its heading (kin.heading) and the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction), read as the dot product of the two normalised vectors, is below minus `cos_tol`, the cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed that still counts as against. Not denoted: occupancy of the carrier, which the caller states; the direction of motion, since a vehicle pointing against the direction points against it whether it moves forwards or backs; travel across the carrier, with headings near perpendicular to it; a carrier with no designated direction, for which the concept is unknown.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "c", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "cos_tol", "unit": "1", "meaning": "Cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed at which a heading still points against the direction."}], "elements": [{"span": "its heading (kin.heading)", "atoms": ["kin.heading"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.heading: 'direction the body points', read normalised."}, {"span": "the carrier's designated direction (st.lane_direction)", "atoms": ["st.lane_direction"], "concepts": [], "justification": "st.lane_direction: 'direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in — a lane ... or a roadway, one-way roadway or shoulder', read normalised; a place no carrier covers has none (unknown)."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car on a one-way roadway points opposite its designated direction."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car points along the roadway's designated direction."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with kin.heading declared absent.", "masked": ["kin.heading"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_227_1_o1"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.left_turn", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user has turned to the left: over the window of length `window` behind the observation, its heading changed to the left (prim.heading_change, left positive) by at least `min_angle` and by less than `max_angle`, the change at which the heading has come round to the opposite direction (a reversal, not a left turn). The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band. The act began within the window behind that observation. The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it. No conduct before the window is read. Not denoted: a right turn; a reversal of direction; a lane change or a bend's drift below `min_angle`; where the turn is made, which the caller states.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "window", "unit": "s", "meaning": "The window over which the heading change is measured: the time within which a turn is completed."}, {"name": "min_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The leftward heading change from which the manoeuvre is a turn."}, {"name": "max_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The leftward heading change from which the heading has come round to the opposite direction (a reversal)."}], "act": {"boundary": "window", "window": "window", "onset": "The act began within the window behind that observation.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band.", "extent": "The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it.", "history": "No conduct before the window is read."}, "elements": [{"span": "its heading changed to the left (prim.heading_change, left positive)", "atoms": ["prim.heading_change"], "concepts": [], "justification": "prim.heading_change: 'the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate; unknown where the window is truncated'."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car turns left at a junction: within the window its heading changes to the left by more than the minimum and well short of a reversal."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car drives straight; its heading change over the window is near zero."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with kin.yaw_rate declared absent, so prim.heading_change is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_227_1_o3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.u_turn", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\": over the window of length `window` behind the observation, the magnitude of its heading change (prim.heading_change, integrated from its yaw rate across forward and backing moves alike) is at least `min_angle` and at most `max_angle`, the band within which its heading has come round to the opposite direction (a smaller change is a turn, a larger one a loop past the opposite direction). The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band. The act began within the window behind that observation. The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it. No conduct before the window is read. Not denoted: a turn short of a reversal; a loop past the opposite direction; where the turn is made, which the caller states; the class of the road user, which the caller states.", "definition": "DEF-NRS-484B-077", "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "window", "unit": "s", "meaning": "The window over which the heading change is measured: the time within which a reversal, in one move or several, is completed."}, {"name": "min_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The heading change magnitude from which the heading has come round to the opposite direction."}, {"name": "max_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The heading change magnitude beyond which the heading has come round past the opposite direction."}], "act": {"boundary": "window", "window": "window", "onset": "The act began within the window behind that observation.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band.", "extent": "The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it.", "history": "No conduct before the window is read."}, "elements": [{"span": "the magnitude of its heading change (prim.heading_change", "atoms": ["prim.heading_change"], "concepts": [], "justification": "prim.heading_change: 'the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate'; integration over forward and backing moves carries 'whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not'."}], "residues": [{"span": "upon a highway", "why": "The place of the turn is the caller's condition: the concept reads the road user's motion only."}, {"span": "of a vehicle", "why": "The class of the road user is the caller's condition, stated with its own admitted aggregate."}], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car makes a three-point turn within the window and ends heading the opposite way."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car turns left at a junction; its heading change stays short of a reversal."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with kin.yaw_rate declared absent.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_227_1_o3"], "supersedes": null}

