d the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate; unknown where the window is truncated'."}], "residues": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A car turns left at a junction: within the window its heading changes to the left by more than the minimum and well short of a reversal."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A car drives straight; its heading change over the window is near zero."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As holds, with kin.yaw_rate declared absent, so prim.heading_change is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_227_1_o3"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.u_turn", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\": over the window of length `window` behind the observation, the magnitude of its heading change (prim.heading_change, integrated from its yaw rate across forward and backing moves alike) is at least `min_angle` and at most `max_angle`, the band within which its heading has come round to the opposite direction (a smaller change is a turn, a larger one a loop past the opposite direction). The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band. The act began within the window behind that observation. The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it. No conduct before the window is read. Not denoted: a turn short of a reversal; a loop past the opposite direction; where the turn is made, which the caller states; the class of the road user, which the caller states.", "definition": "DEF-NRS-484B-077", "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "window", "unit": "s", "meaning": "The window over which the heading change is measured: the time within which a reversal, in one move or several, is completed."}, {"name": "min_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The heading change magnitude from which the heading has come round to the opposite direction."}, {"name": "max_angle", "unit": "deg", "meaning": "The heading change magnitude beyond which the heading has come round past the opposite direction."}], "act": {"boundary": "window", "window": "window", "onset": "The act began within the window behind that observation.", "recognition": "The act is recognized at the observation at which the window's heading change entered that band.", "extent": "The concept holds while the window's change stays in the band, and ends when the change leaves it.", "history": "No conduct before the window 