{"node_id": "LVMC_11_38_030", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-38-030"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle", "ru.moped", "ru.electric_scooter"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "No motorcycle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "or motor scooter", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall be ridden upon any sidewalk", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "of the City", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definitions table admits 'motorcycle' as the aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels in contact with the ground, excluding an electric bicycle, a tractor or a moped'). ru.aggregate is 'membership of a legal aggregate' and is claimed whole, never expanded into ru.motorcycle. Its 'not a stand-in for' clauses do not apply: the words name a class, not a role described by conduct or a relational role. The word 'No' negates the duty the obligation span s3 states."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.moped", "ru.electric_scooter"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Motor scooter' has no applicable definition, so its words are mapped by contract. A scooter driven by a motor is, in the taxonomy the corpus posts, either a moped (DEF-NRS-484A-125: 'a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle' with a small engine; ru.moped: 'a low-power two- or three-wheeler with a small engine or motor, as a jurisdiction classes it') or an electric scooter (DEF-NRS-484A-082: 'a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'; ru.electric_scooter: 'a standing or seated electric scooter with handlebars'). A motor scooter above the moped's power is a motorcycle under DEF-NRS-484A-135 and is carried by s1. The ontology carries no body-style attribute, so a moped of cycle body is re