ewalk is ridden there; a machine pushed along the sidewalk is read the same way.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A motorcycle (ru.motorcycle, an included class of the aggregate) moves along a sidewalk: its footprint overlaps a st.sidewalk region and kin.speed is above the tolerance; asm.within_city_limits is declared true."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same motorcycle moves along the roadway beside the sidewalk; rel.occupies holds for the st.roadway and for no st.sidewalk region; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A bicycle (ru.bicycle: neither in the motorcycle aggregate nor a moped or electric scooter) is ridden along the sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "A motorcycle moves beside a sidewalk; the source declares rel.occupies absent, so whether its footprint overlaps the sidewalk is unknown.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "A motorcycle stands parked on the sidewalk: kin.speed is zero at every observation; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A moped (ru.moped) moves along the sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits true."}, {"name": "branch_3", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A motorcycle moves along a sidewalk; asm.within_city_limits is declared false."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.motion_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Speed resolution: the noise floor of a source's speed estimate, below which a road user is read as standing still.", "source": "Simulator ground-truth and tracker speed-noise figures (a few tenths of a metre per second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "LVMC_11_43_010_A", "law_refs": ["LVMC-11-43-010-A"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The following regulations pertain to the", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "operation of vehicles", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "within a roundabout", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "All vehicular travel", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "shall be in a counterclockwise direction", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The definitions table admits 'vehicle' as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', with its exceptions); ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate', claimed whole. It is not a relational role: 'operation' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.roundabout", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'Roundabout' (DEF-LVMC-11-02-130: 'an intersection characterized by a circulatory roadway, channelized approaches and yield control of entering traffic', encompassing 'the area bounded by the outermost curb line') is st.roundabout: 'a rotary intersection: its central island, its circulatory roadway and its entry and exit approaches'; the atom has no 'not a stand-in for' clause, and the defined word keeps its whole extent, approaches and crosswalks included. 'within' places the subject in the feature: rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.moving"], "justification": "'vehicular' is the admitted vehicle aggregate (claimed whole); 'travel' is the vehicle's motion, drv.motion.moving: in motion beyond the speed resolution. A vehicle standing in 