licy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets, WB-67 design vehicle overall length."}, {"name": "p.caravan_entry_time_headway", "unit": "s", "value": 1.0, "convention": "Minimum accepted lead and lag time gap of a merging or lane-changing vehicle, applied once ahead of and once behind the entering vehicle.", "source": "Lane-change gap-acceptance studies (critical lead and lag gaps of about one second)."}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_210_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-210-3"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not overtake and pass another vehicle upon the right", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "when such movement requires driving off the paved portion of the highway", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole (ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'). 'The driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080) is a relational role, which ru.aggregate is 'not a stand-in for'; it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.interaction.passing_on_right"], "justification": "'overtake and pass ... upon the right' is drv.interaction.passing_on_right(x, y): the two heading the same way, side by side, y on x's left, x gaining on y. 'another vehicle' is the admitted vehicle aggregate, claimed whole, for the road user y passed, quantified inside the obligation (a party present only when one is there)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["st.shoulder", "st.road_edge", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "'driving off the paved portion of the highway' is the vehicle's footprint on an unpaved surface of the way: st.shoulder ('the part of the highway beside the roadway not intended for vehicular traffic; paved attribute') with paved false, or st.road_edge ('curb or edge of the roadway; paved attribute for the surface beyond it') whose surface beyond is unpaved and which the footprint straddles; rel.occupies anchors the subject on that feature. Neither atom carries a 'not a stand-in for' clause. 'requires' is read through the conduct: the movement mad